---
/**
 * Keep inline tags on one line with outer spaces (Astro whitespace).
 * Never break before <em>/<strong>/<a> after a word.
 * No em-dashes in public copy.
 */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ConceptPageHero from '../../components/concepts/ConceptPageHero.astro';
import ConceptPager from '../../components/concepts/ConceptPager.astro';
import { getConcept } from '../../lib/concepts';

const c = getConcept('emergent');
---

<Layout title={`${c.title} | Identity Engineering`}>
	<main class="min-h-screen">
		<ConceptPageHero
			scene={c.scene}
			tag={`${c.tag} · ${c.layerLabel}`}
			title={c.title}
			lede={c.blurb}
			scrollHint={c.scrollHint}
		/>

		<section class="border-t border-white/10 px-6 py-24">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-8 text-lg leading-relaxed text-white/55">
				<div class="mb-2 text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Definition</div>
				<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white md:text-4xl">
					From many to one higher order.
				</h2>
				<p>
					An <strong class="text-white/80">emergent identity</strong> arises when a sufficient number of individual identities interact intensely enough that they stop reading as separate parts and begin to behave as one coherent whole.
				</p>
				<p>
					At a critical region of interaction, a new stable pattern appears that is not reducible to any single participant. The collective develops its own persistence, its own memory, and its own tension continuum. It begins to behave as if it had its own Identity Stem: a recognizable trajectory that persists across changes in its members.
				</p>
				<div class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-black/30 p-6">
					<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[3px] text-white/40 mb-3">Binding is continuous, not a hard switch</div>
					<p class="text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
						In physical binding and continuous phase transitions, potential landscapes are smooth. Bound states become preferred when the effective free energy (or the causal-entropy functional) develops a new minimum. The transition is gradual until a critical region is crossed: the driving force overcomes opposing forces and the system settles into the new basin. Identity Engineering adopts the same stance. We do not posit binary thresholds. We model a continuous binding potential whose critical region marks the shift from temporary coordination to durable higher-order identity.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="border-t border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02] px-6 py-24">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
				<div class="mb-6 text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Mechanics</div>
				<ul class="space-y-6 text-lg text-white/55">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/80">Critical region of emergence:</strong> Intensive, sustained interaction plus shared directional pressure plus persistence under perturbation. Before that region: coordination. Inside and beyond it: a higher-order identity with its own trajectory.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/80">New Tension Continuum:</strong> The collective develops its own high-dimensional tension field with characteristic frequencies and damping requirements.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/80">Dissipative nature:</strong> Maintaining collective coherence requires continuous energy expenditure through norms, institutions, and enforcement.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/80">Higher-order Sameness:</strong> The collective develops its own recognizable trajectory that persists beyond changes in individual members.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="border-t border-white/10 px-6 py-24">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-8 text-lg leading-relaxed text-white/55">
				<div class="mb-2 text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Collective scale</div>
				<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white md:text-4xl">
					Minimal conditions for a durable collective identity
				</h2>
				<p>
					Collective identity is itself an emergent, temporary worldline. This time the bound units are individual Stems, not elementary degrees of freedom.
				</p>
				<ul class="space-y-5">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/80">Binding of degrees of freedom:</strong> Multiple Stems cede relative Access and Jurisdiction to a shared configuration.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/80">Own trajectory:</strong> The collective acquires a recognizable State Differential (shared history) and a Vision Gradient (shared direction of maximal causal entropy).
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/80">Mass accumulation:</strong> The density of bound stake produces emergent Mass, which in turn generates Curvature and Gravitation at the higher scale.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/80">Persistence versus coordination:</strong> Temporary coordination dissolves when binding energy falls below the critical region. Durable collective identity possesses its own damping and survives the turnover of individual participants.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="border-t border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02] px-6 py-24">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-8 text-lg leading-relaxed text-white/55">
				<div class="mb-2 text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Mutual interest</div>
				<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white md:text-4xl">
					What each side gains from the other
				</h2>
				<p>
					The relationship between an individual identity and its associated emergent identity is not zero-sum. It is a geometric efficiency relation.
				</p>
				<div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
					<div class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-black/30 p-6">
						<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[3px] text-white/40 mb-3">Individual receives</div>
						<ul class="space-y-2 text-white/60">
							<li>Stability (reduced external tension, shared damping)</li>
							<li>Amplification of its own direction</li>
							<li>Access to an expanded reachable region of configuration space</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
					<div class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-black/30 p-6">
						<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[3px] text-white/40 mb-3">Emergent receives</div>
						<ul class="space-y-2 text-white/60">
							<li>Mass (bound stake density of participants)</li>
							<li>Rotation (habits of participants as tangential force)</li>
							<li>Lower internal wobble when alignment is high</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
				</div>
				<p>
					Both sides therefore share an interest in high alignment of Vision Gradients and low wobble on both scales. When the emergent direction becomes dominant and stops incorporating the directions of its participant Stems, internal resistance rises. Energy dissipates into friction instead of shared causal entropy. Net output toward emergence falls, and individuals lose the stability and amplification they sought.
				</p>
				<p>
					It is therefore the geometric interest of a healthy emergence to let the full directions of its identities unfold within itself as far as binding allows. That maximizes coherent Mass and usable Rotation while minimizing internal dissipation.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="border-t border-white/10 px-6 py-24">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-white/55">
				<div class="mb-2 text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Ideas as higher-order case</div>
				<p>
					A sufficiently binding, Mass-accumulating idea is a paradigmatic entry into higher-order identity. Organizations are the institutionalized form: idea plus bound configurations (structures) plus living participant Stems. Not every slogan qualifies. The critical region requires persistence, independent trajectory, and causal influence beyond any single carrier.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong class="text-white/80">Engineering implication:</strong> Once a collective crosses into emergence, it develops its own protective and steering mechanisms, most notably higher-order damping, to preserve coherence while keeping future possibilities open. Jurisdiction over the collective Stem must remain accountable to the degrees of freedom of the participants, or the mutual-interest geometry collapses.
				</p>
				<div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-black/30 p-6">
					<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[3px] text-white/40 mb-3">Collective diagnostic prompts</div>
					<ul class="space-y-3 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
						<li>Does the group retain recognizable direction when members rotate out?</li>
						<li>Can the collective absorb shocks without identity collapse?</li>
						<li>Are coordination patterns person-dependent or system-dependent?</li>
						<li>Does the collective Stem still incorporate the Vision Gradients of its participants, or has it become one-way?</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
				<div class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-cyan-400/20 bg-cyan-400/[0.04] p-6 text-base leading-relaxed text-white/60">
					<div class="mb-2 text-sm uppercase tracking-[3px] text-cyan-300/80">Foundations anchor</div>
					<p>
						The dissipative character of emergent collective order (coherence that exists only while continuous energetic and institutional work continues) is rooted in Prigogine’s theory of dissipative structures.
						See <a href="/foundations/prigogine-dissipative-structures" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 underline-offset-4 transition hover:text-white hover:decoration-white/50">Ilya Prigogine: Dissipative Structures and Far-from-Equilibrium Order</a>.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-black/20 p-6 text-base leading-relaxed text-white/55">
					<div class="mb-2 text-sm uppercase tracking-[3px] text-white/40">Open precision work</div>
					<p>
						Formal thresholds, scaling of primitives to collective scale, and the precise binding conditions for ideas-as-identities remain open. See public gaps
						<a href="https://github.com/identity-engineering/framework/issues/60" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 underline-offset-4 transition hover:text-white hover:decoration-white/50" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">#60</a>,
						<a href="https://github.com/identity-engineering/framework/issues/61" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 underline-offset-4 transition hover:text-white hover:decoration-white/50" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">#61</a>,
						<a href="https://github.com/identity-engineering/framework/issues/62" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 underline-offset-4 transition hover:text-white hover:decoration-white/50" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">#62</a>.
						The page-level Critical Gaps block is rendered automatically by the site layout.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<ConceptPager id="emergent" />
	</main>
</Layout>
